@iSazonov In case there is any interest the behavior again in the future, it would probably be best to simply check the event count for each channel and skip adding channels with 0 events to the query. This will cause new events that get logged to one of these empty channels during the query execution to get "missed", but if you consider the design to be to get all the events that were present at the exact moment the user ran the command, this should be fine.

